\f0\fs24 \cf0 Implement the following plan for the Peer Support co-sign review system.\
\
Do not redesign unrelated parts of the application. Preserve existing routes, database structure, queue behavior, signing behavior, authentication, and InSync ingestion unless this plan explicitly changes them.\
\
# PS CO-SIGN REVIEW V2\
\
## Primary objective\
\
Replace the current expensive review pipeline with:\
\
1. Mechanical duplicate awareness\
2. Existing mechanical time and required-field checks\
3. Exactly one AI documentation review per note version\
4. Human review of all mechanical and AI findings together\
\
Duplicate detection must use zero AI calls.\
\
A possible duplicate must not prevent the note from continuing through the AI review. A note may simultaneously have:\
\
- A possible-duplicate flag\
- A time or mechanical warning\
- An AI diagnosis/goal-alignment issue\
- An off-site-rationale issue\
- A peer correction\
- A supervisor-review issue\
\
The purpose is to show the human reviewer every issue during the same review cycle.\
\
--------------------------------------------------\
NON-NEGOTIABLE ARCHITECTURE\
--------------------------------------------------\
\
For every new or revised note:\
\
1. Run mechanical checks.\
2. Run mechanical duplicate comparison.\
3. Run one AI review.\
4. Store all results separately.\
5. Present them together to the human reviewer.\
\
Do not stop the AI review because a possible duplicate was found.\
\
Do not send comparison notes to the AI.\
\
Do not use AI to judge duplication.\
\
Do not make multiple AI calls for different clinical issues.\
\
The off-site analysis, diagnosis alignment, goal alignment, intervention review, client-response review, and reopen-message generation must occur within the same AI call.\
\
An unchanged note that has already been successfully reviewed must not generate another AI call during a later pull.\
\
A revised note is a new note version and receives one new AI review.\
\
Manual \'93Rejudge\'94 generates exactly one new AI call.\
\
--------------------------------------------------\
AI CALL COUNTS\
--------------------------------------------------\
\
Expected call behavior:\
\
- New note: one AI call\
- Revised note: one AI call for the revised version\
- Unchanged note pulled again: zero AI calls\
- Manual rejudge: one AI call\
- Duplicate detection: zero AI calls\
- Mechanical time checks: zero AI calls\
\
Instrument this during testing.\
\
The total automatic AI call count for a pull should equal the number of new or materially changed note-review fingerprints.\
\
--------------------------------------------------\
STEP 1 \'97 MECHANICAL DUPLICATE AWARENESS\
--------------------------------------------------\
\
Relevant files:\
\
- backend/utils/peerSupervisorEngine.js\
- backend/utils/psIngest.js\
\
Remove the AI duplicate judge completely.\
\
Delete or stop using:\
\
- aiCloneJudge\
