- MAX_CANDIDATE_PAIRS\
- ps_prompt_clone in active settings\
- Any Claude call made solely to compare two notes\
\
The old database setting may remain unused. No database cleanup is required.\
\
## Sections to compare\
\
Split the note into these sections:\
\
1. Focus of the meeting:\
2. What activities took place, and for how long?\
3. Peer Support Interventions:\
4. Patient's Response/Content:\
5. Plan:\
\
Compare corresponding sections only:\
\
- Focus against Focus\
- Activities against Activities\
- Intervention against Intervention\
- Response against Response\
- Plan against Plan\
\
Do not compare one section type against another.\
\
Add or adapt:\
\
- SECTION_LABELS\
- splitSections(noteText)\
\
Reuse the existing section-slicing helper where practical.\
\
Bound each section at the next recognized section label.\
\
Bound the Plan section at the existing session-content terminators, including:\
\
- Fxx.x treatment-plan markers\
- Visit Codes\
- Treatment Plan\
- Electronically Signed\
- Provider NPI\
- Other existing session-content terminators already used by the engine\
\
## Similarity mechanics\
\
Reuse the existing mechanical functions:\
\
- normContent\
- bigramMap\
- bigramSimFromMaps\
\
Precompute each corpus note\'92s section text and bigram maps once per pull.\
\
Do not recompute the corpus maps for every comparison.\
\
Skip a section when either side contains fewer than 120 normalized characters.\
\
## Duplicate-awareness threshold\
\
A note should be flagged as a possible duplicate when either condition is met:\
\
A. At least one substantive section is 90% or more similar.\
\
Substantive sections are:\
\
- Focus of the meeting\
- What activities took place, and for how long?\
- Peer Support Interventions\
- Patient's Response/Content\
\
OR:\
\
B. At least two sections are 80% or more similar.\
\
The Plan section may support a duplicate flag but must never trigger a duplicate flag by itself.\
\
Routine headings and standard boilerplate must not independently trigger a possible duplicate.\
\
Return all sections with similarity of at least 80%, even when only one qualifying section triggered the flag.\
\
## Duplicate result shape\
\
Keep the existing `clone` key for backward compatibility, but its result is now entirely mechanical.\
\
Use:\
\
\{\
  "partnerEid": "...",\
  "pct": 94,\
  "reason": "Possible duplicate: Peer Support Interventions is 94% similar to MRN 000123 from 07/14/2026.",\
  "sections": [\
    \{\
      "label": "Peer Support Interventions",\
      "pct": 94\
    \},\
    \{\
      "label": "Patient's Response/Content",\
      "pct": 86\
    \}\
  ],\
  "status": "POSSIBLE_DUPLICATE"\
\}\
\
Use the phrase \'93Possible duplicate,\'94 not \'93Duplicate,\'94 because the human reviewer makes the final determination.\
\
## Comparison pool\
\
For this implementation, preserve the current comparison-pool behavior unless changing it is necessary to make the code function:\
\
- Existing pending notes\
- Notes progressively added during the current ingest batch\
\
Do not add a new historical-note retrieval project in this change.\
\
Signed, reopened, and superseded notes should retain their current inclusion or exclusion behavior.\
\
Update:\
\
- findClone \uc0\u8594  findDupe, or retain the old method name internally if changing it would unnecessarily disrupt callers\
- fullScan\
- ingestQueue\
- rejudge paths\
- partner-flagging logic\
\
There must be no Claude request anywhere in the duplicate-detection path.\
