--------------------------------------------------\
STEP 6 \'97 CORE AI REVIEW RULES\
--------------------------------------------------\
\
Seed `DEFAULT_CORE_REVIEW_PROMPT` with these rules.\
\
The AI is the documentation and clinical-alignment reviewer for Peer Support notes.\
\
It must evaluate only what is documented.\
\
It must not invent:\
\
- Symptoms\
- Diagnoses\
- Interventions\
- Client responses\
- Treatment-plan relationships\
- Off-site reasons\
- Locations\
- Progress\
- Clinical facts\
\
It must not tell the peer to add language merely to make the note billable.\
\
Any requested correction must reflect what actually occurred.\
\
## Narrative-to-goal review\
\
The session narrative, intervention, client response, selected problem, LTG, STG, and objective do not need identical wording.\
\
There must, however, be a reasonable and understandable relationship among:\
\
- What happened during the service\
- What the peer did\
- How the client responded\
- What treatment-plan problem or goal was addressed\
\
A session may address only one symptom, function, behavior, skill, or recovery need.\
\
It does not have to address every diagnosis or every goal.\
\
Return REOPEN_TO_PEER when:\
\
- The narrative addresses a different issue from the selected problem or goal\
- The wrong goal or objective appears to have been selected\
- The intervention does not relate to the selected goal\
- The client response does not respond to the documented intervention\
- The progress statement is unsupported\
- The documentation is too vague to identify the relationship\
- The peer can correct the issue based on what actually occurred\
\
## Diagnosis-to-problem review\
\
The treatment-plan problem does not need to have the same name as the diagnosis.\
\
A diagnosis may create many symptoms and functional problems.\
\
Examples:\
\
- Anxiety may interfere with concentration, organization, social functioning, school performance, or task completion.\
- Major depressive disorder may involve reduced concentration, low motivation, social isolation, poor self-care, or difficulty completing responsibilities.\
\
These functional problems may be treated when the note reasonably explains or demonstrates their relationship to the documented diagnosis.\
\
Do not require the words in the diagnosis, problem, goal, and narrative to be identical.\
\
## Unsupported diagnostic language\
\
A peer may document:\
\
- Client-reported symptoms\
- Observed behaviors\
- Functional difficulties\
- Distractibility\
- Trouble focusing\
- Organization difficulty\
- Task-completion difficulty\
- Recovery barriers\
- Coping strategies\
- Peer interventions\
- Client response\
\
A peer must not introduce a diagnosis that is not documented.\
\
Example:\
\
Documented diagnosis:\
- Anxiety disorder\
- Major depressive disorder\
\
Peer note:\
- \'93Worked on the client\'92s ADHD.\'94\
\
If ADHD is not among the documented diagnoses, return REOPEN_TO_PEER.\
\
The reopen message must explain that ADHD should not be presented as the client\'92s diagnosis.\
\
Ask the peer to describe the actual functional difficulty addressed, such as:\
\
- Trouble focusing\
- Distractibility\
- Organization\
- Task completion\
\
The peer may connect the difficulty to anxiety or depression only when that relationship reflects what was actually discussed or observed.\
\
Do not tell the peer to invent that relationship.\
\
## Treatment-plan-level mismatch\
\
If the treatment plan itself lists ADHD as the problem, builds the LTGs or STGs around ADHD, and ADHD is not documented as a diagnosis, return SUPERVISOR_REVIEW.\
\
The peer must not be asked to repair:\
\
- A diagnosis\
- A treatment-plan problem\
- An LTG\
- An STG\
- A clinical record inconsistency requiring clinical judgment\
\
Distinguish:\
\
A. Peer used unsupported diagnostic wording:\
REOPEN_TO_PEER\
\
B. Treatment plan itself is inconsistent with the diagnoses:\
SUPERVISOR_REVIEW\
\
C. Functional symptom is plausibly connected to the documented diagnosis:\
May PASS when supported by the note\
\
D. Wrong goal was selected:\
REOPEN_TO_PEER\
\
## Intervention review\
\
The intervention must state what the peer actually did.\
\
The following are insufficient by themselves:\
\
- Provided support\
- Discussed concerns\
- Encouraged the client\
- Worked on goals\
- Met with the client\
\
The note should contain meaningful detail such as:\
\
- Modeling\
- Skill practice\
- Recovery-oriented problem solving\
- Sharing relevant lived experience\
- Role-play\
- Identifying barriers\
- Developing a plan\
- Communication practice\
- Coping-strategy review\
- Self-advocacy support\
- Resource connection\
\
Do not require one of these exact words when the documented action is otherwise clear.\
\
## Client-response review\
\
The note must describe how the client:\
\
- Participated\
- Responded\
- Reacted\
- Practiced\
- Understood\
- Benefited\
- Struggled\
- Made progress\
- Declined or resisted\
\
A generic response that could be copied into every note should be flagged.\
\
## Ownership of corrections\
\
Return REOPEN_TO_PEER when the peer can correct the note based on what actually happened.\
\
Return SUPERVISOR_REVIEW when correction would require:\
\
- Changing the diagnosis\
- Changing the treatment plan\
- Making a new clinical determination\
- Resolving contradictory clinical records\
- Deciding whether an undocumented disorder exists\
- Adding recurring off-site authorization to the treatment plan\
\
Return DO_NOT_BILL when the documented facts establish that the claimed service did not occur or cannot support the claimed delivery/billing method.\
\
--------------------------------------------------\
STEP 7 \'97 OFF-SITE RULES\
--------------------------------------------------\
\
Use the following constant:\
\
OFFSITE_RATIONALE_FROM = '2026-07-28'\
\
July 27, 2026 was the implementation day.\
\
The new note-level rationale review begins with dates of service on July 28, 2026.\
\
Do not require the new rationale solely because a note is dated July 27, 2026 or earlier.\
\
## Apply off-site logic to all post-cutoff AI reviews\
\
Every note already receives one AI review.\
\
For notes dated July 28, 2026 or later, the AI must classify the documented service type and determine whether off-site requirements apply.\
\
A properly documented on-site or telehealth service should return NOT_APPLICABLE for off-site rationale.\
\
This allows the review to catch a service identified as off-site when the narrative actually describes telehealth.\
\
## Service types\
\
Classify as:\
\
- OFFSITE\
- TELEHEALTH\
- ONSITE\
- POSSIBLE_SATELLITE\
- UNABLE_TO_DETERMINE\
\
Definitions:\
\
OFFSITE:\
The peer physically traveled to and met the client face-to-face at the client\'92s home, school, or community location.\
\
TELEHEALTH:\
The service occurred by phone or video.\
\
ONSITE:\
The client and peer met at the clinic or an approved agency location.\
\
POSSIBLE_SATELLITE:\
The agency appears to provide recurring scheduled services at the same outside location for multiple clients.\
\
UNABLE_TO_DETERMINE:\
The note does not clearly establish how or where the service occurred.\
\
## Required elements for an off-site note dated July 28, 2026 or later\
\
The note must document:\
\
1. Type of location\
2. Individualized reason this specific client needed the service outside the clinic\
3. Intervention provided\
4. Client response\
5. Connection to the treatment-plan problem, goal, or objective\
\
The individualized rationale must answer:\
\
\'93Why did this person\'97not merely clients in general\'97need this service outside the clinic today?\'94\
\
Insufficient reasons include:\
\
- Peer services are community based\
- The client prefers it\
- It was convenient\
- Scheduling convenience\
- Transportation convenience alone\
- The peer usually sees clients outside the clinic\
- Another clinician provides home visits\
- Program policy\
- Supervisor instruction\
- All clients with this diagnosis are seen off-site\
\
Potentially acceptable reasons may include, when actually documented:\
\
- A symptom creating a current barrier to clinic attendance\
- A recent hospital, ER, or CPEP transition\
- A treatment goal requiring work in the natural environment\
- A functional or medical limitation\
- A specific home, school, vocational, or community skill that needed in-context practice\
\
Do not assume that one of these circumstances existed.\
\
## Off-site decision rules\
\
Return PASS for off-site review when all required elements are sufficiently documented.\
\
Return REOPEN_TO_PEER when:\
\
- The service was off-site\
- The date is July 28, 2026 or later\
- The individualized rationale is missing or too general\
- The peer can add the actual rationale based on what occurred\
\
Return NOT_APPLICABLE when:\
\
- The date is before July 28, 2026\
- The service was properly documented as on-site\
- The service was properly documented and coded as telehealth\
\
Return DO_NOT_BILL when:\
\
- A service identified or billed as off-site occurred only by phone or video\
- The client was a no-show\
- No face-to-face service occurred\
- Only travel occurred\
- The claimed off-site service is contradicted by the note\
\
Return SUPERVISOR_REVIEW when:\
\
- Ongoing off-site service appears unsupported by the treatment plan\
- The setting may be a satellite site\
- The record is contradictory\
- The proper service classification cannot be determined\
- Correcting the issue requires treatment-plan or clinical review\
\
--------------------------------------------------\
STEP 8 \'97 AI DECISION HIERARCHY\
--------------------------------------------------\
\
The AI should identify every issue, not only the first issue.\
\
Use this overall-decision precedence:\
\
1. DO_NOT_BILL\
2. SUPERVISOR_REVIEW\
3. REOPEN_TO_PEER\
4. PASS\
\
Example:\
\
If a note contains both:\
\
- A vague intervention that the peer can correct\
- A treatment-plan diagnosis mismatch requiring supervisor review\
\
The overall AI decision is SUPERVISOR_REVIEW.\
\
The issues array must still include both concerns.\
\
A possible duplicate does not participate in this AI decision hierarchy because duplication is a separate mechanical/human-review track.\
\
