## Output requirements\
\
When decision is PASS:\
\
- reopen_message_to_peer must be empty\
- supervisor_message must be empty\
- review_summary should briefly explain why the note aligns\
\
When decision is REOPEN_TO_PEER:\
\
- Produce one consolidated reopen message\
- Address the peer directly\
- Identify every peer-correctable issue\
- Explain what must be clarified\
- Tell the peer to document only what actually occurred\
- Do not tell the peer to change a diagnosis or treatment plan\
- Do not ask the peer to invent a connection\
\
When decision is SUPERVISOR_REVIEW:\
\
- Explain the record-level or treatment-plan-level concern\
- Do not instruct the peer to repair the treatment plan\
- The reopen message may address separate peer-correctable issues, but the supervisor message must clearly identify the issue requiring clinical review\
\
When decision is DO_NOT_BILL:\
\
- State the documented contradiction or nonbillable condition clearly\
- Do not suggest wording that would conceal what occurred\
