STEP 10 \'97 EXAMPLE REOPEN MESSAGES\
--------------------------------------------------\
\
The prompt should contain examples similar to these.\
\
## Unsupported ADHD wording\
\
\'93The note identifies ADHD as the condition addressed, but ADHD is not listed among the client\'92s documented diagnoses. Please do not describe ADHD as the client\'92s diagnosis. Based on what actually occurred, describe the specific difficulty addressed, such as trouble focusing, distractibility, organization, or task completion, and explain its relationship to the documented diagnosis and selected goal only if that relationship was actually discussed or observed. If the treatment-plan problem itself is incorrect, it must be reviewed by a supervisor.\'94\
\
## Wrong goal selected\
\
\'93The narrative describes work on social isolation, but the selected goal concerns employment skills. Please select the goal that was actually addressed during this session, or correct the narrative if the wrong session information was entered.\'94\
\
## Vague intervention\
\
\'93The intervention states only that support was provided. Please describe what you actually did during the session and how the client responded. Examples may include modeling, skill practice, problem solving, sharing relevant lived experience, role-play, or developing a plan, but include only what actually occurred.\'94\
\
## Missing off-site rationale\
\
\'93Because this off-site service occurred on or after July 28, 2026, the note must explain why this specific client needed the service outside the clinic on this date. Please document the actual clinical or functional reason, the type of location, and how meeting there supported the selected treatment-plan goal. Do not use a general statement that peer services are community based.\'94\
\
Do not include a duplicate reopen message in the AI prompt because duplicate adjudication is human-controlled.\
